%I A399835 #9 Sep 19 2026 17:17:28
%S A399835 1,3,4,5,6,12,8,15,10,18,12,20,14,24,24,31,18,30,20,30,32,36,24,60,26,
%T A399835 42,40,40,30,72,32,63,48,54,48,50,38,60,56,90,42,96,44,60,60,72,48,
%U A399835 124,50,78,72,70,54,120,72,120,80,90,60,120,62,96,80,127,84,144,68,90,96
%N A399835 The sum of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is a powerful number (A001694), where gcud is the greatest common unitary divisor.
%C A399835 First differs from A399836 at n = 64.
%C A399835 The number of these divisors is A399829(n).
%H A399835 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399835/b399835.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A399835 Multiplicative with a(p^2) = p^2 + 1, and a(p^e) = (p^(e+1) - 1)/(p - 1) for e != 2.
%F A399835 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s-1) * zeta(s) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^(2*s-1) + 1/p^(3*s-2) + 1/p^(3*s-1) - 1/p^(4*s-2)).
%F A399835 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ c * n^2 / 2, where c = zeta(2) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^3 + 1/p^4 + 1/p^5 - 1/p^6) = 1.51772844664904399615... .
%t A399835 f[p_, e_] := If[e == 2, p^2 + 1, (p^(e+1)-1)/(p-1)]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A399835 (PARI) a(n) = {my(f = factor(n)); prod(i = 1, #f~, if(f[i,2] == 2, f[i,1]^2 + 1, (f[i,1]^(f[i,2]+1)-1)/(f[i,1]-1)));}
%Y A399835 Cf. A001694, A013661, A077610, A165430, A225174, A384244, A399829.
%Y A399835 The sum of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is: A188999 (1), A399834 (squarefree), this sequence (powerful), A399836 (square), A399837 (exponentially odd), A399838 (odd), A399839 (power of 2).
%K A399835 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A399835 1,2
%A A399835 _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 13 2026
